# 16. ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Do not consider the implementation complete until these tests pass.

### Plan creation and defaults

1. New restaurant receives Flex by default.
2. Flex subscription is stored in the database.
3. Correct 3% commission rate is applied.
4. Plan details remain after refresh and re-login.

### Feature entitlements

5. Flex can use all core ordering features.
6. Flex cannot access Essential-only advanced device management.
7. Essential unlocks staff invitation and remote device revocation.
8. Professional unlocks multi-floor and banquet management.
9. Enterprise unlocks multi-branch and white-label features.
10. Unauthorized API calls are rejected.
11. Frontend cannot override plan entitlements.

### Commission calculations

12. Flex calculates 3% correctly.
13. Essential calculates 2% correctly.
14. Professional calculates 0.75% correctly.
15. Enterprise calculates 0%.
16. Cancelled orders do not generate commission.
17. Partial refunds generate correct adjustments.
18. Duplicate webhooks do not create duplicate commission entries.
19. Historical commission uses the original plan snapshot.

### Billing

20. Paid subscription requires verified payment.
21. Invalid webhook signatures are rejected.
22. Payment failure does not activate a paid plan.
23. Successful payment activates the correct plan.
24. Invoices are generated correctly.
25. Subscription history persists.
26. Cancellation follows the configured policy.
27. Downgrades preserve historical data.

### Tenant isolation

28. Restaurant A cannot view Restaurant B billing records.
29. Restaurant A cannot access Restaurant B commission ledger.
30. Staff cannot change their restaurant subscription.
31. Enterprise branch permissions are enforced.

### User experience

32. Pricing cards show correct information.
33. Feature comparison matches actual entitlements.
34. Upgrade prompts show the correct required plan.
35. Owner can access complete billing history.
36. Dashboard works on mobile and desktop.

